  "details": "When the VRChat camera's FOV is set via OSC, the value doesn't jump to the target instantly. There seems to be an internal smoothing/easing applied to the zoom, so the camera eases toward the requested FOV over a short moment instead of snapping to it.\n\nThis becomes an issue when switching between camera setups that use different FOVs over OSC. The camera position switches instantly, but the FOV lags slightly and eases into place. For filming and cinematography, where you're cutting between shots, this small delay is noticeable and gets in the way of clean transitions.\n\nI'd like one of the following behaviors:\n\n1. When an FOV value is sent over OSC, apply it instantly with no easing, or\n\n2. When the \"Smooth\" option is turned off in the camera's Behaviour tab, have the FOV respond without smoothing as well — so that toggle governs zoom, not just camera movement.\n\nEither option would make it possible to perform clean, instant cuts between different focal lengths via OSC, which matters a lot for camera switching in video production.",
